cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Hydra: a character-level neural lemmatiser and morphological tagger for pre-modern languages"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gagala
    given-names: Lukasz
repository-code: "https://github.com/Lukasz-G/Hydra"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "2.0.0"
keywords:
  - lemmatization
  - part-of-speech tagging
  - historical linguistics
  - Middle High German
  - digital humanities
abstract: >-
  Hydra lemmatises and morphologically tags pre-modern vernaculars from the
  manuscript's own spelling, without a normalisation step or a tokeniser
  fitted to a modern corpus. A character-level temporal convolutional encoder
  feeds a bank of eight parallel decoding slots, so a single written token
  that realises several words is decoded into several lemmas and tags at
  once. It is trained on four reference corpora of historical German and
  reports every figure under a named split protocol.
